{
  "id": "motor-overflow",
  "term": "motor overflow",
  "definition": "Motor overflow is a neuromotor phenomenon in which muscles that are not needed for an intended movement become involuntarily active at the same time. It is understood as a loss of normal inhibitory control within and between the brain’s motor systems, causing motor activity to spread to unintended body areas.",
